@page "/"
@inject LearningHost Host

<PageTitle>Blazor learning sandbox</PageTitle>
<article class="index-page">
    <header class="home-hero">
        <p class="kicker">A lab manual for Blazor and MudBlazor · .NET 10</p>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h1">Learn by changing <em>working</em> examples.</MudText>
        <p class="lede">
            Nine labs explain how Blazor behaves, and why. A gallery shows every MudBlazor component in working
            examples, every parameter combination, and playgrounds that write the markup for you. Complete page samples
            show how the pieces fit together. Read the source beside each one, change one thing, and watch what happens.
        </p>
        <MudStack Row Wrap="Wrap.Wrap" Spacing="2" Class="mt-6">
            <MudButton Href="counter" Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" EndIcon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.ArrowForward">Start with the first lab</MudButton>
            <MudButton Href="components" Variant="Variant.Outlined" Color="Color.Primary">Browse components</MudButton>
            <MudButton Href="samples" Variant="Variant.Text" Color="Color.Primary">See page samples</MudButton>
        </MudStack>
    </header>

    <div class="home-columns">
        <section class="home-column" aria-labelledby="home-labs">
            <p class="home-figure">@LabCatalog.All.Count</p>
            <h2 id="home-labs">Labs</h2>
            <p>State, forms, grids, HTTP, persistence, authentication, localization, files and observability. Each lab states its objective, a common mistake and an exercise.</p>
            <MudLink Href="labs" Typo="Typo.body2">Choose a learning path →</MudLink>
        </section>
        <section class="home-column" aria-labelledby="home-components">
            <p class="home-figure">@GalleryCatalog.Components.Count</p>
            <h2 id="home-components">Components</h2>
            <p>Buttons to data grids to charts. Every example shows the exact Razor that rendered it, and matrices put every variant and color side by side.</p>
            <MudLink Href="components" Typo="Typo.body2">Open the gallery →</MudLink>
        </section>
        <section class="home-column" aria-labelledby="home-samples">
            <p class="home-figure">@GalleryCatalog.Samples.Count</p>
            <h2 id="home-samples">Page samples</h2>
            <p>Dashboards, sign-in, settings, a storefront, a kanban board and more: whole screens composed only from MudBlazor components.</p>
            <MudLink Href="samples" Typo="Typo.body2">See the samples →</MudLink>
        </section>
    </div>

    <MudDivider Class="my-10" />
    <MudGrid Spacing="6">
        <MudItem xs="12" md="7">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mb-3">Run it yourself</MudText>
            <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/jonathanperis/blazor-mudblazor-starter.git
cd blazor-mudblazor-starter
dotnet run --project src/WebClient</code></pre>
            <MudLink Href="https://jonathanperis.github.io/blazor-mudblazor-starter/docs/getting-started/" Typo="Typo.body2">Setup and learning guide →</MudLink>
        </MudItem>
        <MudItem xs="12" md="5">
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mb-3">This host</MudText>
            <MudText Class="mb-2">You are using the <strong>@Host.Name</strong> host.</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Style="color: var(--ink-soft)">Counter and grid experiments reset with their component or @Host.ScopeLifetime. Notebook entries are kept in @Host.NotebookStorage.</MudText>
        </MudItem>
    </MudGrid>
</article>
